package/kernel/mt76: pass CONFIG_MAC80211_DEBUGFS to the driver build

mt76 guards its per-station debugfs hook (drv->sta_add_debugfs and the
mt7915/mt7996 station nodes) with CONFIG_MAC80211_DEBUGFS.  The package
already maps CONFIG_PACKAGE_MAC80211_MESH and CONFIG_PACKAGE_CFG80211_TESTMODE
to the corresponding driver defines, but not the debugfs one, so
CONFIG_PACKAGE_MAC80211_DEBUGFS=y compiles mac80211's station debugfs while
every mt76 per-station node stays out of the module.  Mirror the MESH
handling.  The CR6608 kit's per-peer uplink attribution nodes depend on it;
the build proof step checks the compiled module for them.

--- a/package/kernel/mt76/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/Makefile
@@ -414,6 +414,10 @@ ifdef CONFIG_PACKAGE_MAC80211_MESH
   NOSTDINC_FLAGS += -DCONFIG_MAC80211_MESH
 endif
 
+ifdef CONFIG_PACKAGE_MAC80211_DEBUGFS
+  NOSTDINC_FLAGS += -DCONFIG_MAC80211_DEBUGFS
+endif
+
 ifdef CONFIG_PACKAGE_CFG80211_TESTMODE
   NOSTDINC_FLAGS += -DCONFIG_NL80211_TESTMODE
   PKG_MAKE_FLAGS += CONFIG_NL80211_TESTMODE=y
